# MeritScreen engineering rules

Read existing architecture (`ARCHITECTURE.md`, `docs/01`–`docs/07`) before changing code. Do not rewrite working modules. Prefer extending feature modules over enlarging `:app`.

## Product invariants

- Fail lock is **always device-wide** (all non-emergency apps). Never add a per-app-only fail.
- Child Home and quiz UI read **Room only**. No Firestore, FCM, or AI calls on that path.
- `AppConfig` in `:core:common` is the only place for tunables such as `MAX_CHILDREN_PER_PARENT`. Never scatter those numbers.
- Do not collect GPS, contacts, SMS, photos, or a child email.

## Android / UI

- Kotlin, Jetpack Compose, Material 3, Coroutines, Flow, Hilt.
- Use `:core:ui` tokens. No hard-coded colors.
- Every screen: loading, error (user-facing `AppError`), empty + retry where it applies.
- Avoid extra third-party libraries. No AccessibilityService or hidden APIs to trap users.
- If Android cannot enforce a control, document the limitation instead of faking it.

## Data / Firebase

- Parents access only their family; child custom tokens are scoped to `childId`.
- Enforce authz in security rules, not only in UI.
- Prefer cached Room policy offline; fail closed on integrity errors.
- Review read/write cost before adding listeners. No Home-path listeners.

## Quality

- Separate UI from use cases and repositories.
- Test session/fail-lock and authz first. Use `:core:testing` fakes.
- Never log PIN, tokens, emails, or pairing codes (`LogSanitizer`).
- Update docs when behavior or schema changes.
- A feature is not done until it works end-to-end (UI, logic, backend, states, tests).
